WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.700
A call option allows

2
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.310
an investor to pay a fixed
premium for the right,

3
00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.690
but not the obligation,

4
00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.190
to buy an asset at

5
00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:23.550
a predetermined price
until expiration.

6
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:25.800
The long call strategy might be

7
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.510
useful for an investor who is

8
00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:29.415
bullish on either the markets

9
00:00:29.415 --> 00:00:32.160
or the price of a specific stock.

10
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.490
Investors going long
calls make profits if

11
00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:38.310
the price of the
underlying shares rise

12
00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:40.110
above the combined value of

13
00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:44.615
the strike price and the
net cost of the option.

14
00:00:44.615 --> 00:00:48.365
The payoff from a long call
position is unlimited,

15
00:00:48.365 --> 00:00:50.960
increasing point for
point with the stock

16
00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.505
if the price of the underlying
shares moves higher.

17
00:00:54.505 --> 00:00:57.020
The loss potential is limited

18
00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.705
to the initial cost
of the option.

19
00:00:59.705 --> 00:01:02.900
Investors face a maximum
loss of the premium

20
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.915
and any point at or
below the strike price,

21
00:01:05.915 --> 00:01:09.035
above which point
losses diminish.

22
00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:12.530
The value of a long call option
is hurt by the passage of

23
00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:16.830
time and benefits from
increases in volatility.